{
  "source": {
    "name": "cambra-inspector/examples/polymorphic.chl",
    "text": "# Let-polymorphism + monomorphization. `dup` is used at two distinct types, so\n# inference specializes it into two clones. The post-desugar (pre-inference)\n# body `(x, x)` carries a hole; downstream it resolves to a *set* of tuple types\n# (Int and Bool) — the B5 hole->downstream-type stitch, and the mono fan-out\n# that makes `stageLinks` non-empty.\ndup = \\x -> (x, x)\na = dup(1)\nb = dup(2 == 2)\na\n"
  },
